CONTRACTS
[~] APIRegistry.sol
[~] X402Facilitator.sol
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOG
* Created init APIRegistry.sol & APIRegistry.t.sol
    FUNC:
    - register API
    - store API (bc state)
    - list all API (arr)
    - get API provider
    - update API
    - query API details
    - utils
    LACK:
    - payment enforcement
    - access control for API usage
    - no linkage to payment layer 
    - no ownership transfer / admin ctrl
    - weak api design
* Created init X402Facilitator.sol & X402Facilitator.t.sol
    FUNC:
    - accept payments intent (settle())
    - transfers USDC (ERC20)
    - splits fee (provider and treasury)
    - prevent replays atk
    - checks deadline
    - emits settlement event
    LACK:
    - no real EIP-3009 verification => cryptographic payment protocol
    - no cryptographic binding
    - no authorization proof layer
- Still TODO: X402Facilitator and APIRegistry improvements
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GETTING STARTED
- after cloning this repository, run the following steps:
    1. Move into contracts folder
            cd packages/contracts
    2. Install Foundry dependencies (IMPORTANT)
            forge install
        2.1. This installs forge-std into:
                lib/forge-std
        2.2. If imports fail, run:
                forge install foundry-rs/forge-std
    3. Build contracts
            forge build
    4. Run tests
            forge test -vv
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLEAN SETUP 
- if something breaks
    If forge-std is corrupted:
            rm -rf lib
            forge install
    If cache issues occur:
            forge clean
            forge build
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOCAL BLOCKCHAIN TESTING (ANVIL)
    1. Start local chain
            anvil
    This runs at:
            http://127.0.0.1:8545
    It also prints private keys you can use for testing.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEPLOYMENT FLOW (LOCAL)
    1. Build contracts
            forge build
    2. Deploy using script
            forge script script/Deploy.s.sol \
            --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
            --private-key <ANVIL_PRIVATE_KEY> \
            --broadcast
    This will:
        - compile contracts
        - execute Deploy.s.sol
        - deploy APIRegistry + X402Facilitator
        - print contract addresses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MANUAL TESTING (CAST)
    Register API
            cast send <REGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
            "registerAPI(string,string,uint256)" \
            "BTC API" \
            "https://api.com" \
            1000 \
            --private-key <PRIVATE_KEY> \
            --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545
    Get API
            cast call <REGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
            "getAPI(bytes32)" <API_ID>
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUILD / TEST COMMANDS
    1. Compile
            forge build
    2. Run tests
            forge test
    3. Verbose tests
            forge test -vv
    4. Very verbose (debug)
            forge test -vvvv
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT STRUCTURE
    src/
      APIRegistry.sol      => API discovery => pricing layer
      X402Facilitator.sol  => payment verification => settlement layer
    test/
      APIRegistry.t.sol    => unit tests for registry
    script/
      Deploy.s.sol         => deployment automation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WORKFLOW SUMMARY
1. anvil
2. forge install
3. forge build
4. forge test
5. forge script Deploy.s.sol --broadcast
6. cast send / cast call (manual testing)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES
- forge-std is required for tests and scripts
- All tests run locally in memory (no real blockchain needed)
- Deployment only required for integration or Morph testnet
